  :seon.task/plan "Root's brief 2026-10-23: seon.program-cost-test/recording-a-form-is-flat-in-the-program went red once inside a full bin/test --reach (worktree session SHRINK2, tree ac2743c: 16x bytes and 5-6x ns at every size, REGRESSION past avet-seek-allocates' recorded overrun) and green alone, in the full bin/test right after, and in a later full reach. Measured, not order: the same full reach, same sorted order, every test run (fresh SEON_TEST_RESULTS): 404/404 green; the 21 namespaces before it in one reach process: green; a probe that ran every test in reach's order and after each measured what the process allocated over 100 ms idle found none above 1 MB (no test left a thread or fiber allocating). The cause is in the measurement: seon.profile/alloc-bytes is Chez's (sstats-bytes (statistics)), the whole process's allocation, not the caller's: 1,712 B over 200 ms idle, 1,426,698,112 B over the same 200 ms while one other thread allocates (probe in the test process). Chez has no per-thread count (csug system.stex: bytes-allocated is per generation or total). So a cost proof's bytes (and its time) take in whatever else in the process runs or collects during it: another thread, a fiber, a timer's go block, or a collection's copying (survivors counted again) in a process holding reach's whole program db live. A steady 15x in the minimum of every repeat means something allocated throughout that proof; what it was is not reproduced. The bound is right and stays. Options for root: (a) the harness records the process's allocation while the proof runs that is not the measured call's: measure the same window with the call omitted before and after each size (or the gc-count from (statistics)), and a size measured while the process was not quiet is answered as unmeasured, with the noise as data, never as OVER (seon.cost/judge already has :unmeasured), cheap and honest, but it cannot recover the true number; (b) the true per-thread count, at the cause in the dependency: